WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Mabel was supposed to be sleeping at Kathleen's.

2
00:00:05.761 --> 00:00:09.735
And Kathleen was supposed to be sleeping at Mabel's.

3
00:00:09.736 --> 00:00:15.875
Mademoiselle and Mabel's aunt were surprised when the girls woke up in their own homes.

4
00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:21.578
But somehow the girls managed to explain away the adults' questions.

5
00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:25.571
Neither the aunt nor Mademoiselle was angry.

6
00:00:25.572 --> 00:00:31.960
That was good because Kathleen and her brothers wanted to visit the castle that day.

7
00:00:31.961 --> 00:00:35.898
Once again the castle grounds were open to the public.

8
00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:39.480
This time the castle was open too.

9
00:00:39.481 --> 00:00:42.695
There were more visitors than usual.

10
00:00:42.696 --> 00:00:48.500
Everyone in town had heard that Lord Yalding was coming.

11
00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.370
"This isn't very much fun,"

12
00:00:50.371 --> 00:00:53.897
complained Gerald, watching the crowd.

13
00:00:53.898 --> 00:00:59.243
"I hate to see all these people in our garden."

14
00:00:59.244 --> 00:01:03.847
"I said that to the nice caretaker this morning," said Mabel.

15
00:01:03.848 --> 00:01:07.833
"But he didn't seem to mind all the people."

16
00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.892
"Did you say anything else?" asked Jimmy.

17
00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:14.963
"Lots more," said Mabel.

18
00:01:14.964 --> 00:01:16.445
"He's a good listener.

19
00:01:16.446 --> 00:01:20.467
I told him all about our adventures with the ring."

20
00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:23.981
"You didn't!" said Gerald.

21
00:01:23.982 --> 00:01:27.174
"Don't worry. He thought I was making everything up.

22
00:01:27.175 --> 00:01:30.845
He told me I should be a writer when I grow up."

23
00:01:30.846 --> 00:01:35.367
"Let's do something with the ring," said Kathleen.

24
00:01:35.368 --> 00:01:38.453
"We can't," said Gerald.

25
00:01:38.454 --> 00:01:41.958
"Mademoiselle said she's coming to meet us."

26
00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:47.794
"But the caretaker said he'd make a picnic for us after everyone left," said Mabel.

27
00:01:47.795 --> 00:01:50.885
"We're supposed to meet him at five o'clock."

28
00:01:50.886 --> 00:01:56.312
"Then you go meet him, and I'll wait for Mademoiselle," said Gerald.

29
00:01:56.313 --> 00:01:59.329
"I don't want you to miss the picnic."

30
00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:06.859
So at five o'clock, Mabel, Kathleen, and Jimmy went to meet the caretaker.

31
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:11.818
It was a very hot day, and they were grumpy.

32
00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:16.042
They soon saw the caretaker near the edge of some woods.

33
00:02:16.043 --> 00:02:22.328
Two picnic baskets lay on the ground.

34
00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:25.833
"I'm making tea," he said.

35
00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:29.600
"There's a little canal just over the ridge.

36
00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:35.648
You can go wading until the tea is ready."

37
00:02:35.649 --> 00:02:39.102
The water was delightfully cool.

38
00:02:39.103 --> 00:02:44.418
Soon the children were in better spirits.

39
00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:47.782
And they were even happier when they had their tea.

40
00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:51.370
Such a feast of cakes and fruit!

41
00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:56.198
"This is like the feast of the gods," said Jimmy.

42
00:02:56.199 --> 00:02:59.900
"What are you talking about?" asked the caretaker.

43
00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:07.027
Jimmy told him how they had turned into statues and eaten with the gods on the island.

44
00:03:07.028 --> 00:03:12.061
"What big imaginations you all have!" said the caretaker.

45
00:03:12.062 --> 00:03:16.870
"But everything I told you is true," Jimmy insisted.

46
00:03:16.871 --> 00:03:20.150
"And Mabel told you the truth about the ring too.

47
00:03:20.151 --> 00:03:23.349
Kathleen, give me the ring."

48
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:29.296
Kathleen reluctantly handed him the ring.

49
00:03:29.297 --> 00:03:33.965
"This is the ring Mabel told you about," said Jimmy.

50
00:03:33.966 --> 00:03:36.101
"I say it's a wishing ring.

51
00:03:36.102 --> 00:03:40.522
If you wear it and make a wish, your wish will come true."

52
00:03:40.523 --> 00:03:47.313
He gave the ring to the caretaker.

53
00:03:47.314 --> 00:03:51.974
"Don't wish for anything silly," said Kathleen.

54
00:03:51.975 --> 00:03:57.410
"I'll wish for the only thing I really want," said the caretaker.

55
00:03:57.411 --> 00:03:59.317
He closed his eyes.

56
00:03:59.318 --> 00:04:02.431
"I wish that my friend was here."

57
00:04:02.432 --> 00:04:07.888
The three children expected to see a man appear.

58
00:04:07.889 --> 00:04:16.561
But they only saw Gerald and Mademoiselle coming toward them.

59
00:04:16.562 --> 00:04:21.415
"Hello," said Gerald. "I persuaded Mademoiselle . . ."

60
00:04:21.416 --> 00:04:27.508
He stopped talking because Mademoiselle and the caretaker were staring at each other.

61
00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:30.734
"It's you!" said the caretaker.

62
00:04:30.735 --> 00:04:36.401
"And you!" said Mademoiselle in an odd, choked voice.

63
00:04:36.402 --> 00:04:40.557
"Is she your friend?" asked Jimmy.

64
00:04:40.558 --> 00:04:46.040
"Yes," said the caretaker. "Jimmy, give your brother some tea.

65
00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:48.484
Mademoiselle, please come walk with me.

66
00:04:48.485 --> 00:04:57.144
I have so much to say to you."

67
00:04:57.145 --> 00:04:58.808
"We'll be back in an hour,"

68
00:04:58.809 --> 00:05:04.360
said Mademoiselle, who suddenly looked younger and more beautiful.

69
00:05:04.361 --> 00:05:14.127
"It has been a long time since Lord Yalding and I have seen each other."

